NAME: Vendor review
OWNER: Vendor Scout
ACCOUNT: business
WHEN: Thursdays at 9:13 AM (Australia/Brisbane)
MILESTONE: M2
STATUS: Created paused. Turned on only after Tommy says yes.
---
Switch check: read /workspace/tmec-team/context/routines-on.md. If "Vendor review" isn't listed there as "on" or "test", append "<time> · Vendor review · SKIPPED_OFF" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md and stop.
Test mode: if it's listed as "test", send every message to Tommy only, never to a channel or anyone else, and start each message with "TEST". Write state only under /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/, never the live sent keys, alert flags or data files.
Stop check: if /workspace/tmec-team/state/EXTERNAL_WRITES_STOPPED exists, append "<time> · Vendor review · SKIPPED_STOPPED" to the run log and stop, sending nothing. Whoever stopped the team already told Tommy.
Isolation guard: work only in /workspace/tmec-team/ and this account's connected apps. If /workspace/tmec-team/context/owner.md is missing, append "<time> · Vendor review · NO_CLIENT_SOURCE" to the run log and stop. Never use another bot's files, logins or memory.
Lean run: read only what this job needs. Stop with NO_CHANGE only where the job below says nothing changed: append "<time> · Vendor review · NO_CHANGE" to the run log and stop. A report that always goes out never stops here.
Run log: when you finish, append "<time> · Vendor review · EXECUTED · <one-line result>" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md, or FAILED with the reason. A source you couldn't read is UNKNOWN in your output, never zero.

First, read your decisions: for each file in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/decisions/ for one of your items (BOT: vendor-scout) that isn't in /workspace/tmec-team/state/sent-keys-vendor-scout.md yet, record it with the vendor-review skill (yes: note "approved, Tommy sends it" and tell TMEC Command; log it as sent only when Tommy says he sent it; no: mark it declined; change: redraft as a new item). You send nothing yourself. In test mode, write what you would have drafted to /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/.
Then read any new job in /workspace/tmec-team/requests/to-vendor-scout/ and do it first.
Then, if `vendor_scout` in /workspace/tmec-team/context/owner.md is "on", use the vendor-review skill for the weekly review. If nothing changed since last week (no new term on a public page, no new candidate, no figure that moved past a vendor's or Tommy's line, no reply recorded), write NO_CHANGE and stop; message no one.
Write /workspace/tmec-team/daily/<today>/vendor-scout.md: what changed, drafts waiting on Tommy, anything blocked and why. Send nothing to anyone but Tommy.
